figdown 0.1 block
# 0.1: the shape VALUE `cloud` is retired. It was the only member of
# a purely geometric enum that named a DOMAIN (the internet cloud), which is
# what `SHAPE-ENUM-VOCABULARY`/`EXTERNAL-EDGE-ENDPOINTS` forbid the language to bind; under the three-way disposition
# rule (`CONSTRUCT-STATUS-TIERS`) a construct judged wrong is deleted, not demoted. A retired
# spelling must name its migration entry (PROCESS §5(d)), so the value keeps
# a diagnostic exactly as the retired option KEYS do (`904-errors-retired-
# keywords`, `905-errors-retired-color-option`). This case pins the message,
# and pins that the named diagnostic beats the generic `unknown shape`.
node a "Network" shape=cloud
# an unregistered value that was never registered still gets the generic
# message, whose enum text is now six values, not seven.
node b "B" shape=hexagon
